# Changesets

When you change this repo, **add or update a Changesets fragment** under `.changeset/` as part of the same work — do not leave it for a follow-up.

## When to add a fragment

Add one fragment **per logical change** (one PR may include several), including:

- EE definition (`execution-environment.yml`), collections, dependencies, or base image
- CI/release workflows (`.github/workflows/`, `.github/actions/`)
- Operator-facing docs or release behavior

Skip only pure typo fixes or edits with zero operator/user impact (e.g. local IDE settings).

## How to add it

Create a **unique** file name, e.g. `.changeset/fix-smoke-test-docker-cp.md` (never reuse a name from another version or PR):

```md
---
"ado-ee": patch
---

Short description of what changed and why it matters to operators.
```

Use `patch`, `minor`, or `major` per [docs/RELEASING.md](../docs/RELEASING.md).

## Before finishing

- [ ] Every commit-worthy change in the session has a matching `.changeset/*.md` fragment (except skipped cases above).
- [ ] Fragment filenames are unique and describe the change.
